./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md:9:We take security seriously. Our measures align with what banks use to protect sensitive financial data. We regularly test and update our security to stay ahead of any threats. Plus, we're checked daily by McAfee for extra reassurance against hackers. You can verify our security strength below or on the <a href="https://www.trustedsite.com/verify?host=all.expensify.com&utm_campaign=mfes_redirect&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=mcafeesecure.com">McAfee SECURE site</a>.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-10-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-11-Discover how Expensify safeguards your information below!
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-12-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-13-## The Gold Standard of Security
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-14-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-15-Expensify follows the highest standard of security, known as the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard. This standard is used by major companies like PayPal, Visa, and banks to protect online credit card information. It covers many aspects of how systems work together securely. You can learn more about it on the <a href="https://listings.pcisecuritystandards.org/pci_security/"> PCI-DSS website</a>. And, Expensify is also compliant with SSAE 16!
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-16-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-17-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-18-## Data and Password Encryption
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-19-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-20-When you press 'enter,' your data transforms into a secret code, making it super secure. This happens whether it's moving between your browser and our servers or within our server network. In tech talk, we use HTTPS+TLS for all web connections, ensuring your information is encrypted at every stage of the journey. This means your data is always protected!
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-21-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-22-## Account Safety
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-23-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-24-Protecting your data on our servers is our top priority. We've taken strong measures to ensure your data is safe when it travels between you and us and when it's stored on our servers.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-25-In our first year, we focused on creating a super-reliable, geographically redundant, and PCI compliant data center. This means your data stays safe, and our systems stay up and running.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-26-We use a dual-control key, which only our servers know about. This key is split into two parts and stored in separate secure places, managed by different Expensify employees.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-27-With this setup, sensitive data stays secure and can't be accessed outside our secure servers.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-28-
./docs/articles/new-expensify/settings/Security.md-29-## Our Commitment to GDPR
--
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md:27:- Contact your banking relationship manager and request that your VCF (Variant Call Format) feed be sent directly to Expensify. Feel free to share this information with them: "There is a check box in your bank's Visa Subscription Management portal that they, or their BPS team, can select to enable the feed. This means there is no need for a test file because Visa already has agreements with 3rd parties who receive the files."
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-28-- Ask your bank to send you the "feed filename" OR the raw file information. You'll need the Processor, Financial Institution (Bank), and Company IDs; these are available in Visa Subscription Management if your relationship manager is still looking for them.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-29-- Once you have the file information, send it to us using the submission form [here](https://expensify.typeform.com/to/cGlCAz?typeform-source=community.expensify.com).
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-30-- While you're waiting for your bank, make sure to set up a domain -- it's required for us to be able to add the feed to your account!
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-31-- We will connect the feed once we receive these details and notify you when the feed is enabled.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-32-
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-33-# How to set up an American Express corporate feed
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-34-To begin the process, you'll need to fill out Amex's required forms and send them to Amex so they can start processing your feed. You can download the forms [here](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zqDA_MCk06jk_fWjzx2y0r4gOyAMqKJe/view?usp=sharing).
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-35-
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-36-Below are instructions for filling out each page of the Amex form:
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-37-- PAGE 1
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-38-  - Corporation Name = the legal name of your company on file with American Express
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-39-  - Corporation Address = the legal address of your company
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-40-  - Requested Feed Start Date = the date you want transactional data to start feeding into Expensify. If you'd like historical data, be sure to date back as far as you'd prefer. You must put this date in an international date format (i.e., DD/MM/YY or spelled out January 1, 1900) to ensure the correct date.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-41-  - Requestor Contact = the name of the individual party completing the request
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-42-  - Email address = the email address of the individual party completing the request
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-43-  - Control Account Number = the master or basic control account number corresponding to the cards you'd like to be on the feed. Please note this will not be a credit card number. If you need help with the correct control account number, please contact Amex.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-44-- PAGE 2
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-45-  - No information required
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-46-- PAGE 3
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Commercial-Card-Feeds.md-47-  - Client Registered Name = the legal name of your company on file with American Express
